#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlight Detection Rules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid "This section describes the syntax detection rules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each rule can match zero or more characters at the beginning of the string "
"they are tested against. If the rule matches, the matching characters are "
"assigned the style or <emphasis>attribute</emphasis> defined by the rule, "
"and a rule may ask that the current context is switched."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid "A rule looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;RuleName attribute=&quot;(identifier)&quot; context=&quot;"
"(identifier)&quot; [rule specific attributes] /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>attribute</emphasis> identifies the style to use for matched "
"characters by name, and the <emphasis>context</emphasis> identifies the "
"context to use from here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <emphasis>context</emphasis> can be identified by:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:570
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An <emphasis>identifier</emphasis>, which is the name of the other context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An <emphasis>order</emphasis> telling the engine to stay in the current "
"context (<userinput>#stay</userinput>), or to pop back to a previous context "
"used in the string (<userinput>#pop</userinput>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:577
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To go back more steps, the #pop keyword can be repeated: "
"<userinput>#pop#pop#pop</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An <emphasis>order</emphasis> followed by an exclamation mark (<emphasis>!</"
"emphasis>) and an <emphasis>identifier</emphasis>, which will make the "
"engine first follow the order and then switch to the other context, e.g. "
"<userinput>#pop#pop!OtherContext</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some rules can have <emphasis>child rules</emphasis> which are then "
"evaluated only if the parent rule matched. The entire matched string will be "
"given the attribute defined by the parent rule. A rule with child rules "
"looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;RuleName (attributes)&gt;\n"
"  &lt;ChildRuleName (attributes) /&gt;\n"
"  ...\n"
"&lt;/RuleName&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:596
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Rule specific attributes varies and are described in the following sections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid "Common attributes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:602
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All rules have the following attributes in common and are available whenever "
"<userinput>(common attributes)</userinput> appears. <emphasis>attribute</"
"emphasis> and <emphasis>context</emphasis> are required attributes, all "
"others are optional."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:609
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>attribute</emphasis>: An attribute maps to a defined "
"<emphasis>itemData</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:612
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>context</emphasis>: Specify the context to which the highlighting "
"system switches if the rule matches."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:615
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>beginRegion</emphasis>: Start a code folding block. Default: unset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>endRegion</emphasis>: Close a code folding block. Default: unset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>lookAhead</emphasis>: If <emphasis>true</emphasis>, the "
"highlighting system will not process the matches length. Default: "
"<emphasis>false</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:626
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>firstNonSpace</emphasis>: Match only, if the string is the first "
"non-whitespace in the line. Default: <emphasis>false</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:630
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>column</emphasis>: Match only, if the column matches. Default: "
"unset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dynamic rules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some rules allow the optional attribute <userinput>dynamic</userinput> of "
"type boolean that defaults to <emphasis>false</emphasis>. If dynamic is "
"<emphasis>true</emphasis>, a rule can use placeholders representing the text "
"matched by a <emphasis>regular expression</emphasis> rule that switched to "
"the current context in its <userinput>string</userinput> or <userinput>char</"
"userinput> attributes. In a <userinput>string</userinput>, the placeholder "
"<replaceable>%N</replaceable> (where N is a number) will be replaced with "
"the corresponding capture <replaceable>N</replaceable> from the calling "
"regular expression. In a <userinput>char</userinput> the placeholder must be "
"a number <replaceable>N</replaceable> and it will be replaced with the first "
"character of the corresponding capture <replaceable>N</replaceable> from the "
"calling regular expression. Whenever a rule allows this attribute it will "
"contain a <emphasis>(dynamic)</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:652
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis>dynamic</emphasis>: may be <emphasis>(true|false)</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Rules in Detail"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:661
#, no-c-format
msgid "DetectChar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:663
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Detect a single specific character. Commonly used for example to find the "
"ends of quoted strings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:665
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;DetectChar char=&quot;(character)&quot; (common attributes) (dynamic) /"
"&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:666
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>char</userinput> attribute defines the character to match."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:672
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect2Chars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:674
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect two specific characters in a defined order."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:675
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;Detect2Chars char=&quot;(character)&quot; char1=&quot;(character)&quot; "
"(common attributes) (dynamic) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:676
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>char</userinput> attribute defines the first character to "
"match, <userinput>char1</userinput> the second."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:682
#, no-c-format
msgid "AnyChar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:684
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect one character of a set of specified characters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:685
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;AnyChar String=&quot;(string)&quot; (common attributes) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:686
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>String</userinput> attribute defines the set of characters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:692
#, no-c-format
msgid "StringDetect"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:694
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect an exact string."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:695
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;StringDetect String=&quot;(string)&quot; [insensitive=&quot;true|"
"false&quot;] (common attributes) (dynamic) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:696 development.docbook:712
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>String</userinput> attribute defines the string to match. The "
"<userinput>insensitive</userinput> attribute defaults to <emphasis>false</"
"emphasis> and is passed to the string comparison function. If the value is "
"<emphasis>true</emphasis> insensitive comparing is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:705
#, no-c-format
msgid "WordDetect"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Detect an exact string but additionally require word boundaries such as a "
"dot <userinput>'.'</userinput> or a whitespace on the beginning and the end "
"of the word. Think of <userinput>\\b&lt;string&gt;\\b</userinput> in terms "
"of a regular expression, but it is faster than the rule <userinput>RegExpr</"
"userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:711
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;WordDetect String=&quot;(string)&quot; [insensitive=&quot;true|"
"false&quot;] (common attributes) (dynamic) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:717
#, no-c-format
msgid "Since: Kate 3.5 (KDE 4.5)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:722
#, no-c-format
msgid "RegExpr"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:724
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Do regular expression search."
msgid "Matches against a regular expression."
msgstr "Buscar empregando expresións regulares."

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:725
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;RegExpr String=&quot;(string)&quot; [insensitive=&quot;true|false&quot;] "
"[minimal=&quot;true|false&quot;] (common attributes) (dynamic) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:726
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>String</userinput> attribute defines the regular expression."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:728
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>insensitive</userinput> defaults to <emphasis>false</emphasis> "
"and is passed to the regular expression engine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:731
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>minimal</userinput> defaults to <emphasis>false</emphasis> and is "
"passed to the regular expression engine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:734
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Because the rules are always matched against the beginning of the current "
"string, a regular expression starting with a caret (<literal>^</literal>) "
"indicates that the rule should only be matched against the start of a line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:738
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See <link linkend=\"regular-expressions\">Regular Expressions</link> for "
"more information on those."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:744
#, no-c-format
msgid "keyword"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:746
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect a keyword from a specified list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:747
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;keyword String=&quot;(list name)&quot; (common attributes) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:748
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>String</userinput> attribute identifies the keyword list by "
"name. A list with that name must exist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:750
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The highlighting system processes keyword rules in a very optimized way. "
"This makes it an absolute necessity that any keywords to be matched need to "
"be surrounded by defined delimiters, either implied (the default "
"delimiters), or explicitly specified within the "
"<emphasis>additionalDeliminator</emphasis> property of the "
"<emphasis>keywords</emphasis> tag."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:755
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a keyword to be matched shall contain a delimiter character, this "
"respective character must be added to the <emphasis>weakDeliminator</"
"emphasis> property of the <emphasis>keywords</emphasis> tag. This character "
"will then loose its delimiter property in all <emphasis>keyword</emphasis> "
"rules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:763
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Int</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:765
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "An integer number."
msgid "Detect an integer number."
msgstr "Un número enteiro."

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:766
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;Int (common attributes) (dynamic) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:767
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This rule has no specific attributes. Child rules are typically used to "
"detect combinations of <userinput>L</userinput> and <userinput>U</userinput> "
"after the number, indicating the integer type in program code. Actually all "
"rules are allowed as child rules, though, the <acronym>DTD</acronym> only "
"allows the child rule <userinput>StringDetect</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:772
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following example matches integer numbers follows by the character 'L'."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:773
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;Int attribute=\"Decimal\" context=\"#stay\" &gt;\n"
"  &lt;StringDetect attribute=\"Decimal\" context=\"#stay\" String=\"L\" "
"insensitive=\"true\"/&gt;\n"
"&lt;/Int&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:779
#, no-c-format
msgid "Float"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:781
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect a floating point number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;Float (common attributes) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:783
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This rule has no specific attributes. <userinput>AnyChar</userinput> is "
"allowed as a child rule and typically used to detect combinations, see rule "
"<userinput>Int</userinput> for reference."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:790
#, no-c-format
msgid "HlCOct"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:792
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect an octal point number representation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:793
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;HlCOct (common attributes) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:794 development.docbook:803 development.docbook:812
#: development.docbook:833 development.docbook:900 development.docbook:915
#, no-c-format
msgid "This rule has no specific attributes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:799
#, no-c-format
msgid "HlCHex"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:801
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect a hexadecimal number representation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:802
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;HlCHex (common attributes) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:808
#, no-c-format
msgid "HlCStringChar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:810
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect an escaped character."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:811
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;HlCStringChar (common attributes) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:814
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It matches literal representations of characters commonly used in program "
"code, for example <userinput>\\n</userinput> (newline) or <userinput>\\t</"
"userinput> (TAB)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:818
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following characters will match if they follow a backslash (<literal>\\</"
"literal>): <userinput>abefnrtv&quot;'?\\</userinput>. Additionally, escaped "
"hexadecimal numbers such as for example <userinput>\\xff</userinput> and "
"escaped octal numbers, for example <userinput>\\033</userinput> will match."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:829
#, no-c-format
msgid "HlCChar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:831
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect an C character."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:832
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;HlCChar (common attributes) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:835
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It matches C characters enclosed in a tick (Example: <userinput>'c'</"
"userinput>). The ticks may be a simple character or an escaped character. "
"See HlCStringChar for matched escaped character sequences."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:843
#, no-c-format
msgid "RangeDetect"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:845
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect a string with defined start and end characters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:846
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;RangeDetect char=&quot;(character)&quot;  char1=&quot;(character)&quot; "
"(common attributes) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:847
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>char</userinput> defines the character starting the range, "
"<userinput>char1</userinput> the character ending the range."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:849
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Useful to detect for example small quoted strings and the like, but note "
"that since the highlighting engine works on one line at a time, this will "
"not find strings spanning over a line break."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:856
#, no-c-format
msgid "LineContinue"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:858
#, no-c-format
msgid "Matches a specified char at the end of a line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:859
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;LineContinue (common attributes) [char=\"\\\"] /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:860
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>char</userinput> optional character to match, default is "
"backslash (<userinput>'\\'</userinput>). New since KDE 4.13."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:862
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This rule is useful for switching context at end of line. This is needed for "
"example in C/C++ to continue macros or strings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:868
#, no-c-format
msgid "IncludeRules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:870
#, no-c-format
msgid "Include rules from another context or language/file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:871
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;IncludeRules context=&quot;contextlink&quot; [includeAttrib=&quot;true|"
"false&quot;] /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:873
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <userinput>context</userinput> attribute defines which context to "
"include."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:874
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If it is a simple string it includes all defined rules into the current "
"context, example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:875
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;IncludeRules context=&quot;anotherContext&quot; /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:877
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the string contains a <userinput>##</userinput> the highlight system will "
"look for a context from another language definition with the given name, for "
"example <programlisting>&lt;IncludeRules context=&quot;String##C++&quot; /"
"&gt;</programlisting> would include the context <emphasis>String</emphasis> "
"from the <emphasis>C++</emphasis> highlighting definition."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:884
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <userinput>includeAttrib</userinput> attribute is <emphasis>true</"
"emphasis>, change the destination attribute to the one of the source. This "
"is required to make, for example, commenting work, if text matched by the "
"included context is a different highlight from the host context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:895
#, no-c-format
msgid "DetectSpaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:897
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detect whitespaces."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:898
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;DetectSpaces (common attributes) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:901
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this rule if you know that there can be several whitespaces ahead, for "
"example in the beginning of indented lines. This rule will skip all "
"whitespace at once, instead of testing multiple rules and skipping one at a "
"time due to no match."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: development.docbook:910
#, no-c-format
msgid "DetectIdentifier"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:912
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Detect identifier strings (as a regular expression: [a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:913
#, no-c-format
msgid "&lt;DetectIdentifier (common attributes) /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:916
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this rule to skip a string of word characters at once, rather than "
"testing with multiple rules and skipping one at a time due to no match."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:925
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tips &amp; Tricks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:928
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have understood how the context switching works it will be easy to "
"write highlight definitions. Though you should carefully check what rule you "
"choose in what situation. Regular expressions are very mighty, but they are "
"slow compared to the other rules. So you may consider the following tips."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:936
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you only match two characters use <userinput>Detect2Chars</userinput> "
"instead of <userinput>StringDetect</userinput>. The same applies to "
"<userinput>DetectChar</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:941
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Regular expressions are easy to use but often there is another much faster "
"way to achieve the same result. Consider you only want to match the "
"character <userinput>'#'</userinput> if it is the first character in the "
"line. A regular expression based solution would look like this: "
"<programlisting>&lt;RegExpr attribute=&quot;Macro&quot; context=&quot;"
"macro&quot; String=&quot;^\\s*#&quot; /&gt;</programlisting> You can achieve "
"the same much faster in using: <programlisting>&lt;DetectChar "
"attribute=&quot;Macro&quot; context=&quot;macro&quot; char=&quot;#&quot; "
"firstNonSpace=&quot;true&quot; /&gt;</programlisting> If you want to match "
"the regular expression <userinput>'^#'</userinput> you can still use "
"<userinput>DetectChar</userinput> with the attribute "
"<userinput>column=&quot;0&quot;</userinput>. The attribute "
"<userinput>column</userinput> counts characters, so a tabulator is only one "
"character."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:954
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can switch contexts without processing characters. Assume that you want "
"to switch context when you meet the string <userinput>*/</userinput>, but "
"need to process that string in the next context. The below rule will match, "
"and the <userinput>lookAhead</userinput> attribute will cause the "
"highlighter to keep the matched string for the next context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:959
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;Detect2Chars attribute=&quot;Comment&quot; context=&quot;#pop&quot; "
"char=&quot;*&quot; char1=&quot;/&quot; lookAhead=&quot;true&quot; /&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:963
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use <userinput>DetectSpaces</userinput> if you know that many whitespaces "
"occur."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:966
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use <userinput>DetectIdentifier</userinput> instead of the regular "
"expression <userinput>'[a-zA-Z_]\\w*'</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:969
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use default styles whenever you can. This way the user will find a familiar "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:972
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Look into other XML-files to see how other people implement tricky rules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:975
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can validate every XML file by using the command <command>validatehl.sh "
"language.xsd mySyntax.xml</command>. The files <filename>validatehl.sh</"
"filename> and <filename>language.xsd</filename> are available in <ulink url="
"\"https://commits.kde.org/syntax-highlighting?path=data/schema\">Syntax "
"Highlighting repository</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:983
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you repeat complex regular expression very often you can use "
"<emphasis>ENTITIES</emphasis>. Example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:985
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?&gt;\n"
"&lt;!DOCTYPE language SYSTEM \"language.dtd\"\n"
"[\n"
"        &lt;!ENTITY myref    \"[A-Za-z_:][\\w.:_-]*\"&gt;\n"
"]&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:986
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you can use <emphasis>&amp;myref;</emphasis> instead of the regular "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:998
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scripting with JavaScript"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1000
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Since &kappname; 3.4 in KDE 4.4 the &kappname; editor component is easily "
#| "extensible by writing scripts. The scripting language is ECMAScript "
#| "(widely known as JavaScript). &kappname; supports two kinds of scripts: "
#| "indentation and command line scripts."
msgid ""
"The &kappname; editor component is easily extensible by writing scripts. The "
"scripting language is ECMAScript (widely known as JavaScript). &kappname; "
"supports two kinds of scripts: indentation and command line scripts."
msgstr ""
"Desde a versión 3.4 de &kappname;, incluída na versión 4.4 da colección de "
"software de KDE, pode ampliarse a funcionalidade do compoñente de edición de "
"&kappname; mediante scripts. A linguaxe a empregar para estes scripts é "
"ECMAScript (máis coñecida como JavaScript). &kappname; permite dous tipos de "
"scripts: de sangrado e da liña de ordes."

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:1007
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indentation Scripts"
msgstr "Scripts de sangrado"

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1009
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Indentation scripts - also referred as indenters - automatically indent "
#| "the source code while typing text. As example, after hitting the return-"
#| "key code the indentation level often increases."
msgid ""
"Indentation scripts - also referred as indenters - automatically indent the "
"source code while typing text. As an example, after hitting the return key "
"the indentation level often increases."
msgstr ""
"Os scripts de sangrado axustan o sangrado do código fonte a medida que se "
"escribe. Por exemplo, despois de premer a tecla Intro adoita aumentarse o "
"nivel de sangrado."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1015
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "The following sections describe step by step how to create the skeleton "
#| "for a simple indenter. As first step, create a new <filename>*.js</"
#| "filename> file called e.g. <filename>javascript.js</filename> in the "
#| "local home folder <filename>$KDEHOME/share/apps/katepart/script</"
#| "filename>."
msgid ""
"The following sections describe step by step how to create the skeleton for "
"a simple indenter. As a first step, create a new <filename>*.js</filename> "
"file called &eg; <filename>javascript.js</filename> in the local home folder "
"<filename>$<envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</envar>/katepart5/script/indentation</"
"filename>. Therein, the environment variable <envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</envar> "
"typically expands to either <filename>~/.local</filename> or <filename>~/."
"local/share</filename>."
msgstr ""
"As seguintes seccións describen paso a paso como crear o esqueleto dun "
"script de sangrado sinxelo. O primeiro paso consistirá en crear un ficheiro "
"<filename>*.js</filename> —por exemplo, <filename>javascript.js</filename>— "
"no cartafol <filename>$KDEHOME/share/apps/katepart/script</filename>."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1023
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On &Windows; these files are located in <filename>%USER%\\AppData\\Local"
"\\katepart5\\indentation</filename>. <replaceable>%USERPROFILE%</"
"replaceable> usually expands to <filename>C:\\\\Users\\\\<replaceable>user</"
"replaceable></filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:1027
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Indentation Script Header"
msgstr "Cabeceira"

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1028
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "The header of the file <filename>javascript.js</filename> is embedded in "
#| "a comment and is of the following form <programlisting>\n"
#| "/* kate-script\n"
#| " * name: JavaScript\n"
#| " * author: Example Name &lt;example.name@some.address.org&gt;\n"
#| " * license: BSD\n"
#| " * revision: 1\n"
#| " * kate-version: 3.4\n"
#| " * type: indentation\n"
#| " * required-syntax-style: javascript\n"
#| " * indent-languages: javascript\n"
#| " * priority: 0\n"
#| " * i18n-catalog: mycatalog\n"
#| " *\n"
#| " * A line without colon ':' stops header parsing. That is, you can add "
#| "optional\n"
#| " * text here such as a detailed license.\n"
#| " */\n"
#| "</programlisting> Each entry is explained in detail now:"
msgid ""
"The header of the file <filename>javascript.js</filename> is embedded as "
"JSON at the beginning of the document as follows: <programlisting>\n"
"var katescript = {\n"
"    \"name\": \"JavaScript\",\n"
"    \"author\": \"Example Name &lt;example.name@some.address.org&gt;\",\n"
"    \"license\": \"BSD License\",\n"
"    \"revision\": 1,\n"
"    \"kate-version\": \"5.1\",\n"
"    \"required-syntax-style\": \"javascript\",\n"
"    \"indent-languages\": [\"javascript\"],\n"
"    \"priority\": 0,\n"
"}; // kate-script-header, must be at the start of the file without comments\n"
"</programlisting> Each entry is explained in detail now:"
msgstr ""
"A cabeceira do ficheiro <filename>javascript.js</filename> escríbese nun "
"comentario e ten a seguinte forma: <programlisting>\n"
"/* kate-script\n"
" * name: JavaScript\n"
" * author: Rosalía de Castro &lt;rosaliadecastro@example.com&gt;\n"
" * license: BSD\n"
" * revision: 1\n"
" * kate-version: 3.4\n"
" * type: indentation\n"
" * required-syntax-style: javascript\n"
" * indent-languages: javascript\n"
" * priority: 0\n"
" * i18n-catalog: catálogo_persoal\n"
" *\n"
" * A partir da primeira liña sen dous puntos («:») remata a análise\n"
" * da cabeceira, polo que pode empregar o comentario para\n"
" * texto adicional, como por exemplo detalles sobre a licencia\n"
" * do script.\n"
" */\n"
"</programlisting> A continuación explícanse punto por punto todas as "
"entradas definidas na cabeceira:"

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1035
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal>name</literal> [required]: This is the indenter name that appears "
"in the menu <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Indentation</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> and in the configuration dialog."
msgstr ""
"<literal>name</literal> (obrigatorio). Este é o nome do script de sangrado, "
"o que aparecerá no menú <menuchoice><guimenu>Utilidades</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Sangrado</guimenuitem></menuchoice> e no diálogo de "
"configuración."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1040 development.docbook:1163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal>author</literal> [optional]: The author's name and contact "
"information."
msgstr ""
"<literal>author</literal> (opcional). O nome de autor e a información de "
"contacto."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1043
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<literal>license</literal> [optional]: Short form of the license, such as "
#| "BSD or LGPLv3."
msgid ""
"<literal>license</literal> [optional]: Short form of the license, such as "
"BSD License or LGPLv3."
msgstr ""
"<literal>license</literal> (opcional). Abreviatura da licenza. Por exemplo: "
"BSD ou LGPLv3."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1046 development.docbook:1165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal>revision</literal> [required]: The revision of the script. This "
"number should be increased whenever the script is modified."
msgstr ""
"<literal>revision</literal> (obrigatorio). O número de revisión do script. "
"Este número debería aumentarse cada vez que se modifique o script."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1049 development.docbook:1166
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<literal>kate-version</literal> [required]: Minimal required &kappname; "
#| "version."
msgid ""
"<literal>kate-version</literal> [required]: Minimum required &kappname; "
"version."
msgstr ""
"<literal>kate-version</literal> (obrigatorio). A versión mínima de "
"&kappname; necesaria para empregar o script."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1052
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<literal>required-syntax-style</literal> [optional]: Comma separated list "
#| "of required syntax highlighting styles. This is important for indenters "
#| "that rely on specific highlight information in the document. If a "
#| "required syntax style is specified, the indenter is available only when "
#| "the appropriate highlighter is active. This prevents <quote>undefined "
#| "behavior</quote> caused by using the indenter without the expected "
#| "highlighting schema. For instance, the Ruby indenter makes use of this in "
#| "the files <filename>ruby.js</filename> and <filename>ruby.xml</filename>."
msgid ""
"<literal>required-syntax-style</literal> [optional]: The required syntax "
"style, which matches the specified <literal>style</literal> in syntax "
"highlighting files. This is important for indenters that rely on specific "
"highlight information in the document. If a required syntax style is "
"specified, the indenter is available only when the appropriate highlighter "
"is active. This prevents <quote>undefined behavior</quote> caused by using "
"the indenter without the expected highlighting schema. For instance, the "
"Ruby indenter makes use of this in the files <filename>ruby.js</filename> "
"and <filename>ruby.xml</filename>."
msgstr ""
"<literal>required-syntax-style</literal> (opcional). Lista, separada por "
"comas, de estilos de realzado de sintaxe que o script necesita. Isto é "
"importante para aqueles scripts que dependen de información de realzado "
"específica no documento. De indicarse un estilo de sintaxe necesario, o "
"script de sangrado só estará dispoñíbel cando ese script de realzado estea "
"activo. Así se evitan <quote>comportamentos inesperados</quote>, causados "
"polo uso de scripts de sangrado sen o esquema de realzado do que estes "
"dependen. Por exemplo, o script de sangrado de Ruby emprega esta opción nos "
"ficheiros <filename>ruby.js</filename> e <filename>ruby.xml</filename>."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1055
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<literal>indent-languages</literal> [optional]: Comma separated list of "
#| "syntax styles the indenter can indent correctly, e.g.: c++, java."
msgid ""
"<literal>indent-languages</literal> [optional]: JSON array of syntax styles "
"the indenter can indent correctly, &eg;: <literal>[\"c++\", \"java\"]</"
"literal>."
msgstr ""
"<literal>indent-languages</literal> (opcional). Lista, separada por comas, "
"de estilos de realzado que o script pode sangrar correctamente. Por exemplo: "
"c++, java."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1058
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal>priority</literal> [optional]: If several indenters are suited for "
"a certain highlighted file, the priority decides which indenter is chosen as "
"default indenter."
msgstr ""
"<literal>priority</literal> (opcional). Se existen varios scripts de "
"sangrado axeitados para un ficheiro de realzado concreto, o valor desta "
"opción, a prioridade, determina cal dos scripts de sangrado se escolle de "
"maneira predeterminada."

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:1067
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Indenter Source Code"
msgstr "Código"

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1068
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Having specified the header this section explains how the indentation "
#| "scripting itself works. The basic skeleton of the body looks like this: "
#| "<programlisting>\n"
#| "triggerCharacters = \"{}/:;\";\n"
#| "function indent(line, indentWidth, ch)\n"
#| "{\n"
#| "    // called for each newline (ch == '\\n') and all characters specified "
#| "in\n"
#| "    // the global variable triggerCharacters. When calling "
#| "<menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Align</guimenuitem></"
#| "menuchoice>\n"
#| "    // the variable ch is empty, i.e. ch == ''.\n"
#| "    //\n"
#| "    // see also: Scripting API\n"
#| "    return -2;\n"
#| "}\n"
#| "</programlisting> The function <function>indent()</function> has three "
#| "parameters: <itemizedlist> <listitem><para><literal>line</literal>: the "
#| "line that has to be indented</para></listitem> "
#| "<listitem><para><literal>indentWidth</literal>: the indentation width in "
#| "amount of spaces</para></listitem> <listitem><para><literal>ch</literal>: "
#| "either a newline character (<literal>ch == '\\n'</literal>), the trigger "
#| "character specified in <literal>triggerCharacters</literal> or empty if "
#| "the user invoked the action <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</"
#| "guimenu><guimenuitem>Align</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.</para></listitem> "
#| "</itemizedlist> The return value of the <function>indent()</function> "
#| "function specifies how the line will be indented. If the return value is "
#| "a simple integer number, it is interpreted as follows: <itemizedlist> "
#| "<listitem><para>return value <literal>-2</literal>: do nothing</para></"
#| "listitem> <listitem><para>return value <literal>-1</literal>: keep "
#| "indentation (searches for previous non-blank line)</para></listitem> "
#| "<listitem><para>return value <literal> 0</literal>: numbers &gt;= 0 "
#| "specify the indentation depth in spaces</para></listitem> </itemizedlist> "
#| "Alternatively, an array of two elements can be returned: <itemizedlist> "
#| "<listitem><para><literal>return [ indent, align ];</literal></para></"
#| "listitem> </itemizedlist> In this case, the first element is the "
#| "indentation depth like above with the same meaning of the special values. "
#| "However, the second element is an absolute value representing a column "
#| "for <quote>alignment</quote>. If this value is higher than the indent "
#| "value, the difference represents a number of spaces to be added after the "
#| "indentation of the first parameter. Otherwise, the second number is "
#| "ignored. Using tabs and spaces for indentation is often referred to as "
#| "<quote>mixed mode</quote>."
msgid ""
"Having specified the header this section explains how the indentation "
"scripting itself works. The basic skeleton of the body looks like this: "
"<programlisting>\n"
"// required katepart js libraries, e.g. range.js if you use Range\n"
"require (\"range.js\");\n"
"  \n"
"triggerCharacters = \"{}/:;\";\n"
"function indent(line, indentWidth, ch)\n"
"{\n"
"    // called for each newline (ch == '\\n') and all characters specified "
"in\n"
"    // the global variable triggerCharacters. When calling "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Align</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>\n"
"    // the variable ch is empty, i.e. ch == ''.\n"
"    //\n"
"    // see also: Scripting API\n"
"    return -2;\n"
"}\n"
"</programlisting> The function <function>indent()</function> has three "
"parameters: <itemizedlist> <listitem><para><literal>line</literal>: the line "
"that has to be indented</para></listitem> "
"<listitem><para><literal>indentWidth</literal>: the indentation width in "
"number of spaces</para></listitem> <listitem><para><literal>ch</literal>: "
"either a newline character (<literal>ch == '\\n'</literal>), the trigger "
"character specified in <literal>triggerCharacters</literal> or empty if the "
"user invoked the action <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Align</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.</para></listitem> </"
"itemizedlist> The return value of the <function>indent()</function> function "
"specifies how the line will be indented. If the return value is a simple "
"integer number, it is interpreted as follows: <itemizedlist> "
"<listitem><para>return value <literal>-2</literal>: do nothing</para></"
"listitem> <listitem><para>return value <literal>-1</literal>: keep "
"indentation (searches for previous non-blank line)</para></listitem> "
"<listitem><para>return value <literal> 0</literal>: numbers &gt;= 0 specify "
"the indentation depth in spaces</para></listitem> </itemizedlist> "
"Alternatively, an array of two elements can be returned: <itemizedlist> "
"<listitem><para><literal>return [ indent, align ];</literal></para></"
"listitem> </itemizedlist> In this case, the first element is the indentation "
"depth as above with the same meaning of the special values. However, the "
"second element is an absolute value representing a column for "
"<quote>alignment</quote>. If this value is higher than the indent value, the "
"difference represents a number of spaces to be added after the indentation "
"of the first parameter. Otherwise, the second number is ignored. Using tabs "
"and spaces for indentation is often referred to as <quote>mixed mode</quote>."
msgstr ""
"Unha vez escrita a cabeceira, é hora de escribir o código que determina a "
"lóxica do script de sangrado. O esqueleto básico do corpo ten o seguinte "
"aspecto: <programlisting>\n"
"triggerCharacters = \"{}/:;\";\n"
"function indent(line, indentWidth, ch)\n"
"{\n"
"    // Esta función execútase para cada nova liña (ch == '\\n') e para\n"
"    // todos os caracteres indicados na variábel global triggerCharacters.\n"
"    // Cando se executa <menuchoice><guimenu>Utilidades</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Aliñar</guimenuitem></menuchoice>\n"
"    // o parámetro ch chega baleiro, é dicir, ch == ''.\n"
"    //     // Vexa tamén a información da sección «API para scripts», máis "
"abaixo.    return -2;\n"
"}\n"
"</programlisting>  A función <function>indent()</function> recibe tres "
"parámetros: <itemizedlist>   <listitem><para><literal>line</literal>. A liña "
"cuxo sangrado debe axustarse.</para></listitem>   "
"<listitem><para><literal>indentWidth</literal>. A anchura do sangrado, "
"medida en cantidade de espazos.</para></listitem>   "
"<listitem><para><literal>ch</literal>. Un carácter de salto de liña "
"(<literal>ch == '\\n'</literal>), o carácter disparador indicado en "
"<literal>triggerCharacters</literal> ou unha cadea baleira se o usuario "
"executou a acción <menuchoice><guimenu>Utilidades</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Aliñar</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.</para></listitem> </"
"itemizedlist>  O valor que devolva a función <function>indent()</function> "
"determinará o sangrado da liña. De tratarse dun número enteiro, "
"interpretarase da seguinte maneira: <itemizedlist>   "
"<listitem><para><literal>-2</literal>. Non facer nada.</para></listitem>   "
"<listitem><para><literal>-1</literal>. Manter o sangrado da primeira liña "
"non baleira anterior á actual.</para></listitem>   <listitem><para><literal> "
"0</literal>. Os números positivos, incluído o 0, indican o nivel de sangrado "
"a aplicar á liña, en espazos.</para></listitem> </itemizedlist> En vez dun "
"enteiro, é posíbel devolver unha matriz de dous elementos: <itemizedlist>   "
"<listitem><para><literal>[ sangrado, aliñación ];</literal></para></"
"listitem> </itemizedlist> Neste caso, o primeiro elemento correspóndese co "
"nivel de sangrado, igual que cando se devolve un número enteiro. Pola outra "
"banda, o segundo elemento é un valor absoluto que representa a columna para "
"a <quote>aliñación</quote>. Se o valor é superior ao valor de sangrado, a "
"diferencia representa un número de espazos a engadir tras o sangrado do "
"primeiro parámetro (o <quote>sangrado</quote>). En caso contrario, este "
"segundo número ignorarase. Ao uso de tabulacións e espazos para o sangrado "
"adoita chamárselle <quote>modo mixto</quote>."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Consider the following example: Assume using tabs to indent, and tab width "
"is set to 4. Here, &lt;tab&gt; represents a tab and '.' a space: "
"<programlisting>\n"
"1: &lt;tab&gt;&lt;tab&gt;foobar(\"hello\",\n"
"2: &lt;tab&gt;&lt;tab&gt;.......\"world\");\n"
"</programlisting> When indenting line 2, the <function>indent()</function> "
"function returns [8, 15]. As result, two tabs are inserted to indent to "
"column 8, and 7 spaces are added to align the second parameter under the "
"first, so that it stays aligned if the file is viewed with a different tab "
"width."
msgstr ""
"Digamos, por exemplo, que estamos a empregar tabulacións para o sangrado, e "
"que a anchura das tabulacións é 4. Aquí, &lt;tab&gt; representa unha "
"tabulación e «.» un espazo: <programlisting>\n"
"1: &lt;tab&gt;&lt;tab&gt;funcion(\"Ola,\",\n"
"2: &lt;tab&gt;&lt;tab&gt;....…\"mundo!\");\n"
"</programlisting> Ao estabelecerse o sangrado da liña 2, a función "
"<function>indent()</function> devolve [8, 15]. Como resultado, insírense "
"dúas tabulacións para levar o sangrado ata a columna 8, e 7 espazos para "
"aliñar o segundo parámetro baixo o primeiro, de xeito que ambos permanezan "
"aliñados independentemente da anchura que os distintos editores de textos "
"cos que se abra o ficheiro empreguen para as tabulacións."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1110
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "A default KDE installation ships &kappname; with several indenters. The "
#| "corresponding JavaScript source code can be found in <filename>$KDEDIR/"
#| "share/apps/katepart/script</filename>."
msgid ""
"A default &kde; installation ships &kappname; with several indenters. The "
"corresponding JavaScript source code can be found in <filename>"
"$<envar>XDG_DATA_DIRS</envar>/katepart5/script/indentation</filename>."
msgstr ""
"A instalación predeterminada da colección de software de KDE fornece varios "
"scripts de sangrado para &kappname;. O seu código fonte está dispoñíbel no "
"cartafol <filename>$KDEDIR/share/apps/katepart/script</filename>."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On &Windows; these files are located in <filename>%USER%\\AppData\\Local"
"\\katepart5\\indentation</filename>. <replaceable>%USER%</replaceable> "
"usually expands to <filename>C:\\\\Users\\\\<replaceable>user</replaceable></"
"filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1117
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Developing an indenter requires to reload the scripts to see whether the "
#| "changes behave appropriately. Instead of restarting the application, "
#| "simply switch to the command line and invoke the command <command>reload-"
#| "scripts</command>."
msgid ""
"Developing an indenter requires reloading the scripts to see whether the "
"changes behave appropriately. Instead of restarting the application, simply "
"switch to the command line and invoke the command <command>reload-scripts</"
"command>."
msgstr ""
"Ao desenvolver un script de sangrado, é necesario recargar os scripts para "
"comprobar se os cambios funcionan como se espera. En vez de reiniciar o "
"aplicativo, é posíbel recargalos empregando a orde <command>reload-scripts</"
"command> desde a liña de ordes."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1123 development.docbook:1229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you develop useful scripts please consider contributing to the &kappname; "
"Project by <ulink url=\"mailto:kwrite-devel@kde.org\">contacting the mailing "
"list</ulink>."
msgstr ""
"Se desenvolve scripts útiles, considere a posibilidade de doalos ao Proxecto "
"&kappname;. Pode contactar connosco (en inglés) mediante a nosa <ulink url="
"\"mailto:kwrite-devel@kde.org\">lista de correo</ulink>."

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:1132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Line Scripts"
msgstr "Scripts da liña de ordes"

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1134
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "As it is hard to satisfy everyone's needs, &kappname; supports little "
#| "helper tools for quick text manipulation through the <link linkend="
#| "\"advanced-editing-tools-commandline\">built-in command line</link>. For "
#| "instance, the command <command>sort</command> is implemented as script. "
#| "This section explains how to create <filename>*.js</filename> files to "
#| "extend &kappname; with arbitrary helper scripts."
msgid ""
"As it is hard to satisfy everyone's needs, &kappname; supports little helper "
"tools for quick text manipulation through the <link linkend=\"advanced-"
"editing-tools-commandline\">built-in command line</link>. For instance, the "
"command <command>sort</command> is implemented as a script. This section "
"explains how to create <filename>*.js</filename> files to extend &kappname; "
"with arbitrary helper scripts."
msgstr ""
"Dado o difícil que resulta compracer a todos, &kappname; permite a "
"definición de pequenas ferramentas de asistencia para a manipulación rápida "
"de texto mediante a <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-tools-commandline"
"\">liña de ordes integrada</link>. Por exemplo, a orde <command>sort</"
"command> fornécea un script. Esta sección explica como crear ficheiros "
"<filename>*.js</filename> para ampliar &kappname; con scripts de asistencia "
"adicionais."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1143
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Command line scripts are located in the same folder as indentation "
#| "scripts. So as first step, create a new <filename>*.js</filename> file "
#| "called <filename>myutils.js</filename> in the local home folder <filename>"
#| "$KDEHOME/share/apps/katepart/script</filename>."
msgid ""
"Command line scripts are located in the same folder as indentation scripts. "
"So as a first step, create a new <filename>*.js</filename> file called "
"<filename>myutils.js</filename> in the local home folder <filename>"
"$<envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</envar>/katepart5/script/commands</filename>. Therein, "
"the environment variable <envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</envar> typically expands to "
"either <filename>~/.local</filename> or <filename>~/.local/share</filename>."
msgstr ""
"Os scripts da liña de ordes están no mesmo cartafol que os scripts de "
"sangrado. Por tanto, o primeiro paso consistirá en crear un novo ficheiro "
"<filename>*.js</filename> (por exemplo, <filename>utilidades.js</filename>) "
"no cartafol <filename>$KDEHOME/share/apps/katepart/script</filename>."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On &Windows; these files are located in <filename>%USER%\\AppData\\Local"
"\\katepart5\\commands</filename>. <replaceable>%USER%</replaceable> usually "
"expands to <filename>C:\\\\Users\\\\<replaceable>user</replaceable></"
"filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:1155
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Command Line Script Header"
msgstr "A cabeceira do script da liña de ordes"

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1156
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "The header of the file <filename>javascript.js</filename> is embedded in "
#| "a comment and is of the following form <programlisting>\n"
#| "/* kate-script\n"
#| " * name: JavaScript\n"
#| " * author: Example Name &lt;example.name@some.address.org&gt;\n"
#| " * license: BSD\n"
#| " * revision: 1\n"
#| " * kate-version: 3.4\n"
#| " * type: indentation\n"
#| " * required-syntax-style: javascript\n"
#| " * indent-languages: javascript\n"
#| " * priority: 0\n"
#| " * i18n-catalog: mycatalog\n"
#| " *\n"
#| " * A line without colon ':' stops header parsing. That is, you can add "
#| "optional\n"
#| " * text here such as a detailed license.\n"
#| " */\n"
#| "</programlisting> Each entry is explained in detail now:"
msgid ""
"The header of each command line script is embedded in JSON at the beginning "
"of the script as follows: <programlisting>\n"
"var katescript = {\n"
"    \"author\": \"Example Name &lt;example.name@some.address.org&gt;\",\n"
"    \"license\": \"LGPLv2+\",\n"
"    \"revision\": 1,\n"
"    \"kate-version\": \"5.1\",\n"
"    \"functions\": [\"sort\", \"moveLinesDown\"],\n"
"    \"actions\": [\n"
"        {   \"function\": \"sort\",\n"
"            \"name\": \"Sort Selected Text\",\n"
"            \"category\": \"Editing\",\n"
"            \"interactive\": \"false\"\n"
"        },\n"
"        {   \"function\": \"moveLinesDown\",\n"
"            \"name\": \"Move Lines Down\",\n"
"            \"category\": \"Editing\",\n"
"            \"shortcut\": \"Ctrl+Shift+Down\",\n"
"            \"interactive\": \"false\"\n"
"        }\n"
"    ]\n"
"}; // kate-script-header, must be at the start of the file without comments\n"
"</programlisting> Each entry is explained in detail now:"
msgstr ""
"A cabeceira do ficheiro <filename>javascript.js</filename> escríbese nun "
"comentario e ten a seguinte forma: <programlisting>\n"
"/* kate-script\n"
" * name: JavaScript\n"
" * author: Rosalía de Castro &lt;rosaliadecastro@example.com&gt;\n"
" * license: BSD\n"
" * revision: 1\n"
" * kate-version: 3.4\n"
" * type: indentation\n"
" * required-syntax-style: javascript\n"
" * indent-languages: javascript\n"
" * priority: 0\n"
" * i18n-catalog: catálogo_persoal\n"
" *\n"
" * A partir da primeira liña sen dous puntos («:») remata a análise\n"
" * da cabeceira, polo que pode empregar o comentario para\n"
" * texto adicional, como por exemplo detalles sobre a licencia\n"
" * do script.\n"
" */\n"
"</programlisting> A continuación explícanse punto por punto todas as "
"entradas definidas na cabeceira:"

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1164
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<literal>license</literal> [optional]: Short form of the license, such as "
#| "BSD or LGPLv3."
msgid ""
"<literal>license</literal> [optional]: Short form of the license, such as "
"BSD License or LGPLv2."
msgstr ""
"<literal>license</literal> (opcional). Abreviatura da licenza. Por exemplo: "
"BSD ou LGPLv3."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1167
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<literal>functions</literal> [required]: Comma separated list of commands "
#| "in the script."
msgid ""
"<literal>functions</literal> [required]: JSON array of commands in the "
"script."
msgstr ""
"<literal>functions</literal> (obrigatorio). Lista de ordes definidas no "
"script, separadas por comas."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal>actions</literal> [optional]: JSON Array of JSON objects that "
"defines the actions that appear in the application menu. Detailed "
"information is provided in the section <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-"
"tools-commandline\">Binding Shortcuts</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since the value of <literal>functions</literal> is a JSON array, a single "
"script is able to contain an arbitrary number of command line commands. Each "
"function is available through &kappname;'s <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-"
"tools-commandline\">built-in command line</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:1180
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Script Source Code"
msgstr "Código"

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1182
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "All functions specified in the header have to be implemented in the "
#| "script. For instance, the script file from the example above needs to "
#| "implement the two functions <command>sort</command> and <command>format-"
#| "paragraph</command>. All functions have the following syntax:"
msgid ""
"All functions specified in the header have to be implemented in the script. "
"For instance, the script file from the example above needs to implement the "
"two functions <command>sort</command> and <command>moveLinesDown</command>. "
"All functions have the following syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Todas as funcións indicadas na cabeceira deben estar definidas no script. "
"Por exemplo, o script do exemplo anterior debe fornecer o código das "
"funcións <command>sort</command> e <command>format-paragraph</command>. "
"Todas as funcións empregan a seguinte sintaxe:"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: development.docbook:1188
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "function &lt;name&gt;(arg1, arg2, ...)\n"
#| "{\n"
#| "    // ... implementation, see also: Scripting API\n"
#| "}"
msgid ""
"// required katepart js libraries, e.g. range.js if you use Range\n"
"require (\"range.js\");\n"
"\n"
"function &lt;name&gt;(arg1, arg2, ...)\n"
"{\n"
"    // ... implementation, see also: Scripting API\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"function &lt;nome&gt;(arg1, arg2, …)\n"
"{\n"
"    // Código.\n"
"    // Vexa tamén a información da sección «API para scripts», máis abaixo.\n"
"}"

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1191
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Arguments in the command line are passed to the function as "
#| "<parameter>arg1</parameter>, <parameter>arg2</parameter>, etc. In order "
#| "to provide documentation for each command, simply implement the "
#| "'<function>help</function>' function as follows: <programlisting>\n"
#| "function help(cmd)\n"
#| "{\n"
#| "    if (cmd == \"sort\") {\n"
#| "        return i18n(\"Sort the selected text.\");\n"
#| "    } else if (cmd == \"...\") {\n"
#| "        // ...\n"
#| "    }\n"
#| "}\n"
#| "</programlisting> Executing <command>help sort</command> in the command "
#| "line then calls this help function with the argument <parameter>cmd</"
#| "parameter> set to the given command, i.e. <parameter>cmd == \"sort\"</"
#| "parameter>. &kappname; then presents the returned text as documentation "
#| "to the user. Make sure to <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-tools-"
#| "scripting-api-i18n\">translate the strings</link>."
msgid ""
"Arguments in the command line are passed to the function as <parameter>arg1</"
"parameter>, <parameter>arg2</parameter>, etc. In order to provide "
"documentation for each command, simply implement the '<function>help</"
"function>' function as follows: <programlisting>\n"
"function help(cmd)\n"
"{\n"
"    if (cmd == \"sort\") {\n"
"        return i18n(\"Sort the selected text.\");\n"
"    } else if (cmd == \"...\") {\n"
"        // ...\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"</programlisting> Executing <command>help sort</command> in the command line "
"then calls this help function with the argument <parameter>cmd</parameter> "
"set to the given command, &ie; <parameter>cmd == \"sort\"</parameter>. "
"&kappname; then presents the returned text as documentation to the user. "
"Make sure to <link linkend=\"dev-scripting-api-i18n\">translate the strings</"
"link>."
msgstr ""
"Os argumentos da liña de ordes envíanse ás funcións como <parameter>arg1</"
"parameter>, <parameter>arg2</parameter>, etc. Para fornecer documentación "
"para as ordes, defina a función «<function>help</function>» da seguinte "
"maneira: <programlisting>\n"
"function help(cmd)\n"
"{\n"
"    if (cmd == \"sort\") {\n"
"        return i18n(\"Ordenar o texto seleccionado.\");\n"
"    } else if (cmd == \"…\") {\n"
"        // …\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"</programlisting> Ao executar <command>help sort</command> na liña de ordes, "
"chámase a esta función co argumento <parameter>cmd</parameter> contendo o "
"nome do parámetro (<parameter>cmd == \"sort\"</parameter>). &kappname; "
"presenta entón o texto devolto como documentación, que o usuario pode ler. "
"Asegúrese de <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-tools-scripting-api-i18n"
"\">internacionalizar as cadeas</link>."

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1206
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Developing a command line script requires to reload the scripts to see "
#| "whether the changes behave appropriately. Instead of restarting the "
#| "application, simply switch to the command line and invoke the command "
#| "<command>reload-scripts</command>."
msgid ""
"Developing a command line script requires reloading the scripts to see "
"whether the changes behave appropriately. Instead of restarting the "
"application, simply switch to the command line and invoke the command "
"<command>reload-scripts</command>."
msgstr ""
"Ao desenvolver un script da liña de ordes, é necesario recargar os scripts "
"para comprobar se os cambios funcionan como se espera. En vez de reiniciar o "
"aplicativo, é posíbel recargalos empregando a orde <command>reload-scripts</"
"command> desde a liña de ordes."

#. Tag: title
#: development.docbook:1213
#, no-c-format
msgid "Binding Shortcuts"
msgstr "Asignación de atallos"

#. Tag: para
#: development.docbook:1214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to make the scripts accessible in the application menu and assign "
"shortcuts, the script needs to provide an appropriate script header. In the "
"above example, both functions <literal>sort</literal> and "
"<literal>moveLinesDown</literal> appear in the menu due to the following "
"part in the script header: <programlisting>\n"
"var katescript = {\n"
"    ...\n"
"    \"actions\": [\n"
"        {   \"function\": \"sort\",\n"
"            \"name\": \"Sort Selected Text\",\n"
"            \"icon\": \"\",\n"
"            \"category\": \"Editing\",\n"
"            \"interactive\": \"false\"\n"
"        },\n"
"        {   \"function\": \"moveLinesDown\",\n"
"            \"name\": \"Move Lines Down\",\n"
"            \"icon\": \"\",\n"
"            \"category\": \"Editing\",\n"
"            \"shortcut\": \"Ctrl+Shift+Down\",\n"
"            \"interactive\": \"false\"\n"
"        }\n"
"    ]\n"
"};\n"
"</programlisting> The fields for one action are as follows:"
msgstr ""

